ng over j and differentiating the finite Frobenius energy sum gives ∫e_t=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). N002 identifies E′ with ∫e_t, proving N003.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"N002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M007\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ,V=ℝ,μ=Lebesgue,f=∂_j g_j.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Euclidean opens measurable.\\\",\\\"ℝ is a normed additive commutative group.\\\",\\\"Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets.\\\",\\\"∂_j g_j is continuous and compactly supported.\\\",\\\"ℝⁿ is the measurable topological space.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝ^(n−1),β=ℝ,μ=ν=Lebesgue,V=ℝ,f=coordinate-permuted ∂_j g_j.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Euclidean factors are measurable and their Lebesgue measures are S-finite.\\\",\\\"ℝ is a real normed space.\\\",\\\"The integrand is continuous compactly supported, so M001 gives product integrability.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M007\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"A=ℝ,a=−L,b=L,f=g_j along a coordinate line,v=1,f′=∂_j g_j,v′=0.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"ℝ has the complete normed ring and real algebra structures.\\\",\\\"g_j and 1 are continuous on uIcc(−L,L).\\\",\\\"Their derivatives are as stated on the open interval.\\\",\\\"The derivatives are continuous and interval-integrable.\\\"]}]}}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{